=== plain-80: width 80, height 24, profile notty, dark, glyphs ascii, plain
# logs pager-commands ------------------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Inferred from v0.3.2 and origin/main. What each pager$
# treatment would run, by the environment. Under sudo, sudo-rs$
# and doas PAGER is dropped [I; not run for PAGER]. pager-env$
# runs as root whatever a kept PAGER names, and most has its own$
# shell escape [I]. LESSSECURE=1 is less(1)'s secure mode,$
# turning off ! and | and v [unverified: not run]. BusyBox's$
# less reads no LESSSECURE and has no secure mode, and its s and$
# E keys write and open any path as root (miscutils/less.c;$
# read, not run). The gallery's table: nothing runs.$
$
# pager-less, proposed -----------------------------------------$
$
   -  root login, PAGER=most$
      LESSSECURE=1 less /var/log/hardn.log$
   -  sudo, PAGER dropped$
      LESSSECURE=1 less /var/log/hardn.log$
   -  sudo-rs, PAGER dropped [I]$
      LESSSECURE=1 less /var/log/hardn.log$
   -  doas, BusyBox's less$
      None: BusyBox's has no secure mode$
   -  doas, the less package$
      LESSSECURE=1 less /var/log/hardn.log$
   -  sudo, PAGER=most kept$
      LESSSECURE=1 less /var/log/hardn.log$
   -  no less, no PAGER$
      None: the last lines alone$
$
# pager-env, P-18 as written -----------------------------------$
$
   -  root login, PAGER=most$
      most /var/log/hardn.log$
   -  sudo, PAGER dropped$
      LESSSECURE=1 less /var/log/hardn.log$
   -  sudo-rs, PAGER dropped [I]$
      LESSSECURE=1 less /var/log/hardn.log$
   -  doas, BusyBox's less$
      less /var/log/hardn.log$
   -  doas, the less package$
      LESSSECURE=1 less /var/log/hardn.log$
   -  sudo, PAGER=most kept$
      most /var/log/hardn.log$
   -  no less, no PAGER$
      None: the last lines alone$
$
$

